## 2026-08-31

### Project Update

- Implemented an automated canary evaluation step in the Actions workflow: after a staged canary deploy the CI now pulls Prometheus-format metrics from the canary endpoint and runs a small validator that checks error-rate and p95 latency against configurable thresholds. If thresholds are exceeded the workflow will mark the run and trigger the defined rollback job (manual override available).
- Added a secrets-handling prototype and documentation: created a reusable GitHub Actions secrets template and included integration notes and example scripts for HashiCorp Vault token retrieval to avoid embedding deploy credentials in workflows. README now lists required secrets and a quick setup checklist for maintainers.
- Enhanced canary test coverage and tooling: introduced a deterministic traffic simulator that exercises feature-flagged routes under controlled traffic weights and a CI smoke test that validates metrics emission and structured logs. Also added stub tests and issues to track future service-mesh (Istio/linkerd) integration for real-weight routing.
- Operational improvements and runbook updates: expanded the rollback and on-call runbook with steps to inspect metrics, evaluate the validator output, manually promote/cut traffic, and collect troubleshooting artifacts (logs, traces, metric snapshots). Included example kubectl/helm commands and sample Prometheus alert rules to help first responders.
- Next steps: wire the metric-evaluator to alerting channels for automated paging thresholds, add a scheduled job to run dependency-update PRs, and build the full traffic-router integration to enable true weighted traffic shifting and more realistic canary experiments.